  "privacy_title": "Privacy policy",
  "privacy_reading_title": "Reading needs no account",
  "privacy_reading_body": "The mushaf, search, tajweed, tafsirs and recitations work without signing up. Saved pages, your last page and your downloads stay on your device only.",
  "privacy_account_title": "Competition account",
  "privacy_account_body": "To play we keep your email, your name, your password (hashed) and your match results, for your stats and the leaderboard. We never sell or share your data.",
  "privacy_media_title": "Audio and video",
  "privacy_media_body": "In remote matches your microphone and camera stream live to the other participants only when you turn them on. Nothing is recorded or stored.",
  "privacy_delete_title": "Deleting your data",
  "privacy_delete_body": "You can delete your account at any time from your profile. Your email, name and password are removed; match results stay without your name.",
  "sources_title": "Content sources",
  "sources_body": "Quran text: Tanzil project (tanzil.net), Hafs.\nTafsirs, translations and recitations: alquran.cloud and islamic.network.\nAt-Tafsir Al-Muyassar: King Fahd Complex for the Printing of the Holy Quran.\nFonts: Amiri Quran and IBM Plex Sans Arabic, SIL Open Font License.",
  "rules_title": "How to play",
  "rules_overview_title": "The match",
  "rules_overview": "Two players and a referee; {rounds} rounds of {perRound} questions each.\nThe referee prepares the match, choosing its questions or leaving them random, then publishes it so players can enter with its ID.\nPlay in the same room, or remotely with audio and video.",
  "rules_players": "For players",
  "rules_referee": "Referee",
  "rules_what_do_you_know": "A question with many answers; players name them in turns.\nNo timer: the referee moves on whenever ready.\nEach player has one pass per question: with no answer, the turn goes to the opponent without a strike.\nEach player has {strikes} mistakes per question; the last one makes the opponent win: {cleanPoints} with no mistakes of their own, otherwise {points}.",
  "referee_what_do_you_know": "Read the question; tap Correct for each right answer or Wrong for a mistake, and the turn passes automatically. If the player asks to pass, tap Pass (once per player). Move on when you see fit.",
  "rules_ayah_number": "The first ayah of a page is shown; each player secretly writes how many ayahs the page has, within {time}.\nThe exact count wins {points}, otherwise the closest.\nIf both are exact, the faster one scores; if both wrote the same wrong number, nobody scores.",
  "referee_ayah_number": "Read the ayah aloud; once both have written their count, tap Reveal answers.",
  "rules_auction": "A category with a known number of ayahs, shown to both; bids are open and in turn: one player opens (at random on the first question, then alternating) and the other answers.\nEvery bid must beat the last one and restarts the clock ({bid}); bidding the full total ends the bidding.\nA player can say \"go ahead\" and the highest bidder recites; the same happens when time runs out.\nThe bidder names them within {recite}: completing it scores 1 point under 20, 2 from 20, 3 from 30, and so on; otherwise the opponent scores {points}.",
  "referee_auction": "Announce the category and follow the bids; you can end them with Close bidding. Then tap Correct if the player completes the bid, or Wrong.",
  "rules_similar": "An opening shared by several places is shown; there is no buzzer: either player answers aloud.\nA correct answer within {fast} is worth {fastPoints}, within {slow} {slowPoints}, after that nobody scores.\nEach player has {strikes} mistakes; after that they may not answer.",
  "referee_similar": "Read the opening; when one of them answers, tap Correct or Wrong under their name.",
  "rules_buzzer": "The question is hidden from players and audience; the referee reads it aloud.\nThe first to press the buzzer within {time} answers; a correct answer is worth {points}.\nIf wrong, the full question is shown to everyone and the opponent answers; if they are wrong too, nobody scores.",
  "referee_buzzer": "Read the question clearly (only you can see it), then judge whoever buzzed first with Correct or Wrong.",
  "rules_referee_general_title": "For the referee, every round",
  "rules_referee_general": "You can always tap Alternative question to swap it; players see it is an alternative, and points already given for it are taken back.\nYou can always tap Next question; if it wasn't decided, nobody scores.\nYou start the match once both players are in.",
